    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0712" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/2498a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of the American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to Mr. John C. Traphagen of the Foreign Bondholders Protective
                    Council</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-03">May 3, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Traphagen</hi>: There is enclosed herewith a
                    copy of a memorandum entitled “Proposal for Settlement of Direct Funded Debt of
                    Colombia.” The bases suggested in the attached memorandum differ slightly from
                    those discussed when you were here last Saturday. As I informed your Secretary
                    over the telephone today, I would be glad to talk with you about this on the
                    telephone at your convenience.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>


                <xi:include href="d835-a1.xml" xpointer="d835-a1"/>
